dwm - dynamic window manager
============================

Personal dwm build for X. Configuration lives in `config.def.h`; `config.h` is the generated/local build copy.

Build and install
-----------------

    make clean
    rm -f config.h
    make
    sudo make install

Run from `.xinitrc`:

    exec dwm

Mint / Void sessions
--------------------

The binary is independent of the distribution and session launcher. On Mint,
install libx11-dev, libxft-dev, libxinerama-dev, libx11-xcb-dev and
libxcb-res0-dev plus a compiler/make and fontconfig/FreeType headers. On Void,
the corresponding libraries are libX11-devel, libXft-devel, libXinerama-devel,
libxcb-devel, fontconfig-devel and freetype-devel.

Optional bindings need brightnessctl, awk, playerctl, scrot and PipeWire's wpctl.
The polkit agent, screen locker and status process are session responsibilities,
not programs started by dwm. Suspend does NOT lock the screen.

The separate configure-sl checkout supplies an optional dwm-session
launcher for both LightDM and startx. Use its argument-free desktop Exec entry:
put quoted font arguments inside the launcher, not through Xsession's command
string expansion. This repository's make install never registers a session.

Local changes
-------------

- Bar fallback is monospace:size=11; the external session launcher reads
  dwm.font from Xresources and passes -fn. No hardcoded menu-font override:
  dmenu_run and help/tag menus use dmenu-font when installed (plain dmenu fallback).
  Set machine fonts in ~/.config/X11/machine.resources; see configure-sl README.
- Tags can be renamed at runtime with `Super+N`. The labeled dmenu prompt
  runs asynchronously: dwm continues processing events while it is open.
  Enter confirms; Escape cancels. Only one rename runs at a time, and it
  applies to the tags selected when the prompt opened, even if the view changes.
  dmenu still grabs the keyboard while open; if it hangs, killing dmenu from
  a text console/SSH releases that grab. This does not fix an X/input freeze.
- Pertag layout state.
- Window swallowing support plus `dwm-spawn` helper.
- Ghostty terminal launcher and centered floating `st` launcher.
- Brave browser and pcmanfm launchers.
- Audio, media, brightness, screenshot, and suspend key bindings.
- Brightness keys select adjacent absolute levels: 1, 2000, 8000, 16000,
  32000, 64000, and the device maximum (96000 on this machine).
  Levels above the maximum are skipped. Down never turns the backlight off.
  Keep the level lists in both brightness helpers synchronized.
  Disable competing ACPI brightness handlers when dwm owns the brightness keys;
  otherwise a single press can trigger two conflicting backlight changes.
- `dwm-suspend` uses `systemctl suspend` with running systemd, or `loginctl suspend` with identifiable elogind; backend failures are not retried.
- `dwm-keymap` dmenu cheat sheet on `Super+Shift+K`.

Key documentation
-----------------

Press `Super+Shift+K` to open the searchable keymap. Type to filter (smart case: lowercase ignores case; uppercase matches case), use PageUp/PageDown to page, and Escape to close. Launchable entries run after selection.

The help uses 24 rows and full monitor width, preserving the configured menu font.
The old centered menu requested 37 rows plus the prompt without a screen-height
limit, and capped width at 900 pixels: large fonts clipped both ends vertically
and truncated words horizontally. For smaller screens or larger fonts, try
`DWM_KEYMAP_LINES=8 dwm-keymap`. A general dmenu fix would clamp row count to the
selected monitor height and size centered width to the longest entry (bounded by
monitor width). dmenu does not wrap entries; filter to narrow the list, or use a
wrapping terminal pager for long-form help. `Super+Shift+H` opens the st pager;
PageUp/PageDown scroll, `/` searches with smart case, `q` closes.
The keymap requires this local dmenu's `-s` option; the st pager uses `less -i`. Its long lines wrap even when
LESS normally enables horizontal chopping.

Maintenance rule: any change to dwm key/button bindings, or to st-reflow shortcuts shown in the help, must update `dwm-keymap` in the same change.

Common bindings:

- `Super+Shift+P`: application launcher
- `Super+Return`: st terminal
- `Super+Shift+Return`: Kitty terminal
- `Super+Ctrl+Shift+Return`: Ghostty terminal
- `Super+S`: suspend
- `Super+Shift+S`: centered floating st terminal
- `Super+Shift+B`: browser
- `Super+B`: toggle bar
- `Super+Shift+E`: file manager
- `Super+J/K`: focus next/previous client
- `Super+H/L`: shrink/grow master area
- `Super+T/F/M`: tile/floating/monocle
- `Super+Q`: close focused window
- `Super+Shift+Q`: quit dwm
- `Print`: screenshot region/window
- `Shift+Print`: screenshot full screen
